# Copy to .env.local. Never commit .env.local — these are database credentials.
#
# Supabase, created in an EU region (ADR-0020 §4: personal data of Spanish
# shoppers does not leave the union because of where we chose to deploy; ADR-0021
# §3: one vendor holds the data and the identities, so the DPA names one
# sub-processor). Project settings → Database → Connection string.
#
# TWO strings, and they are not interchangeable.

# Transaction pooler, port 6543. What the running app uses: a request checks a
# connection out, runs, gives it back. `prepare: false` in src/db/client.ts goes
# with this — prepared statements cannot survive a pooled connection being reused.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres.PROJECT:PASSWORD@aws-0-eu-central-1.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres"

# Direct connection, port 5432. What `pnpm db:migrate` uses: DDL through a
# transaction pooler is a way to spend an afternoon.
DIRECT_URL="postgresql://postgres.PROJECT:PASSWORD@aws-0-eu-central-1.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres"
